      "intentional_changes": [
        "Implement the existing neutral SearchBackend interface with real native traversal/matching, using one retained FileSearchOwner per provider instead of a controlled test backend.",
        "Atomically reserve provider session slots and aggregate entry/byte/dedicated-worker allowances with checked monotonic identities before admitted startup; release reservations only after Joined cleanup and before publishing the receipt.",
        "Retain startup, close and provider shutdown tasks and first operation/cleanup failures separately; last public lease/provider drop requests cleanup without internal tasks preventing that drop.",
        "Preconstruct full task guards and explicitly move them into async bodies before awaiting. The tracker token is the final guard field so cancellation bookkeeping precedes task-tracker release.",
        "Add a private create_backend policy route for native output limits while preserving legacy and index-only bounded constructors."
      ],
      "ownership": "Provider owns aggregate accounting, retained native owner and task tracker; session owners keep actual native joins. Unconfirmed cleanup quarantines reservations, and lost task receipts cannot be relabeled Joined.",
      "limits": [
        "This establishes real native behavior behind the trait, not a separately packaged worker or production consumer selection.",
        "Retained tasks require a live cooperative runtime; the implementation does not promise interruption of arbitrary filesystem operations or universal OOM/process-abort recovery."
